{"questions":[{"question_id":"1lg0x8s3g","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2007 Paper 1 Offline","year":2007,"examDate":2007,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"electrochemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"conductance-and-electrolysis","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pthe-total-number-of-moles-of-chlorine-gas-evolved-isp-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-pxa8xlge8bilrdkn","content":"<p>The total number of moles of chlorine gas evolved is :</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"0.5"},{"identifier":"B","content":"1.0"},{"identifier":"C","content":"2.0"},{"identifier":"D","content":"3.0"}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<p>Moles of NaCl = 4 <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0.02ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.09ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -491 778 482\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> 0.5 = 2 moles (Since 500 ml = 0.5 L)</p>\n<p>2 moles of NaCl = 2 moles of Cl<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: 0;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.432ex\" height=\"1.754ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -775.2 633.1 775.2\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msup\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(33,363) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>2Cl<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><